      "difficulty_level": "H3",
      "difficulty_reason": "The new counted claim requires one sequence of finite Markovization sets to work for an uncountable time family without continuity or non-atomicity assumptions. Individual pairwise compactness and the previously examined ordinary concatenation continuity do not suffice. The proof combines monotone level-kernel completion and a common countable diagonal selection with an atomic covariance criterion ensuring that quantile pushforward preserves the necessary finite-chain factorization even at omitted times. These mechanisms supply a substantive research-level simultaneous process construction, beyond the old existence/minimal-pair-coupling theorem and beyond the low-difficulty continuity lemma.",
